cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AFFIX-2026, please cite it as below."
title: "AFFIX-2026: Agent Framework Fitness Index eXtended"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Arjun
date-released: "2026-10-22"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  AFFIX-2026 is a comparative evaluation of production-relevant LLM and agent
  application frameworks. Frameworks are scored on a weighted composite
  (AFFIX) across ten dimensions and seven proprietary indices, including
  Rewrite Hazard Score (RHS). Scores are estimates (EST) adjudicated from
  primary documentation and API reality, not marketing claims.
keywords:
  - agent frameworks
  - LLM tooling
  - software engineering
  - lock-in
  - rewrite hazard
  - benchmark
